parisons use the mode-conditioned structural operands.\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No crash, on-disk store or user Restore is exercised.\\\",\n    \\\"The long run commits ordinary command entries only; no further membership change is made during it.\\\",\n    \\\"No repository test was executed.\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"cluster_ids\\\":\\\"A,B,C,D,E\\\",\\\"initial_configuration\\\":\\\"A,B,C\\\",\\\"added_voters\\\":\\\"D,E\\\",\\\"partition\\\":\\\"A,C | B,D,E\\\",\\\"modes\\\":[\\\"defect_restart\\\",\\\"control_no_restore\\\"],\\\"long_run_entries\\\":200,\\\"minimum_entries_after_conflict\\\":150}},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The helper builds five InmemTransports in a full mesh with per-node InmemStore, InmemCommitTrackingStore and InmemSnapshotStore and Config with TrailingLogs 0, bootstraps {A,B,C} from A, starts A, B and C with MockFSM and the feature enabled, elects a leader, transfers leadership to A if needed, applies three commands, waits for A to apply, takes a user snapshot on A, starts D and E, adds each as voter, applies one further command and emits 'fixture'. It shuts A down, cuts {A,C} from {B,D,E}, reconnects A to C only, restarts A with the mode's feature setting and emits 'restart'. It waits for a leader in each partition, applies one write on each leader, reads the entries at the shared index and emits 'outcome'. It reconnects the mesh, waits for one leader, applies one more entry, then applies 200 further entries on that leader and waits (bounded by 15s) until the leader's log has advanced at least 150 entries past the conflict index; only then does it sample payloads and terms at the conflict index, differences in the applied write lists, each node's configuration and the long-run operands, and emit 'healed'. A repair phase follows as before: choose a current-configuration leader, cut A off, apply ten commands, snapshot the leader, reconnect A, wait for the snapshot install and emit 'repaired'. The test runs mode defect_restart first and control_no_restore second. Event order: fixture, restart, outcome, healed, repaired, fixture, restart, outcome, healed, repaired.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"hashicorp/raft configuration scan with the RestoreCommittedLogs replay, and the AppendEntries duplicate-skip that prevents later replication from repairing the divergent entry or refreshing the configuration.\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"fixture\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}]+fx},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"adm_control\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"fixture\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"control_no_restore\\\"}]+fx}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   c(\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"defect_restart\\\",\\\"entry_consistent_at_conflict_index\\\",True,\\\"Feature on, after ~200 further committed entries: all nodes should hold the same entry at the conflict index.\\\"),\n   c(\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"defect_restart\\\",\\\"a_config_ids_after_heal\\\",\\\"A,B,C,D,E\\\",\\\"Feature on, after the long run: the restarted node should use the committed configuration.\\\"),\n   c(\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"defect_restart\\\",\\\"long_run_exercised\\\",True,\\\"Operand: the sample really was taken after at least 150 entries past the conflict index.\\\"),\n   c(\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"defect_restart\\\",\\\"a_log_advanced_after_heal\\\",True,\\\"Operand: the restarted node kept receiving entries, so the persistence is not a stalled node.\\\"),\n   c(\\\"adm_control\\\",\\\"control_no_restore\\\",\\\"entry_consistent_at_conflict_index\\\",True,\\\"Feature off control after the same long run: entries should be consistent.\\\"),\n   c(\\\"adm_control\\\",\\\"control_no_restore\\\",\\\"a_config_ids_after_heal\\\",\\\"A,B,C,D,E\\\",\\\"Feature off control after the long run: the restarted node should use the committed configuration.\\\")]\n }}\njso